{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1096218-atmosphere-and-prop-usage","id":1096218,"title":"Atmosphere and prop usage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-24T04:02:28-07:00","id":1096218,"title":"Atmosphere and prop usage","content":"So this is more of a general question.... Does anyone use candles or dimming lights for atmosphere? What kind of music best fits Prometheans theme of isolation and reconciliation? Any prop usage during games? I don't want it too distracting, but I would like to add to the mood for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T04:05:21-07:00","id":1096222,"title":"","content":"I'd use music. Pick theme songs for particular, important npcs. Candles are fire hazards, and dimming the lights to the point where you can't see your sheet is counterproductive. But there's a point when you put in the npc song before you narrate their appearance and the light up in recognition of your players will feel amazing.<br /> <br /> Oh, table rule? Put the cellphones in a basket. Nothing cuts immersion like having your players constantly checking FB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T04:14:16-07:00","id":1096225,"title":"","content":"Any music that you can suggest? Usually just using Lustmord for ambience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T09:02:44-07:00","id":1097149,"title":"","content":"Penny Dreadful has a lush emotional bleakness - and yes, lush bleakness is a contradiction, but one it pulls off very well - that works for Promethean.<br /> <br /> I second not dimming lights. At any level low enough to be atmospheric, it has far too much risk of becoming annoying instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T10:41:37-07:00","id":1097175,"title":"","content":"Lighting depends entirely on the scene in question and what setup you have available. For aggressive isolation combined with exposure, the old floodlight from above in a dark room (classic interrogation scene) works great, but you can't always pull that off in a home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}